🚦 Road Sign Classifier

A deep learning-based Road Sign Classifier that identifies and classifies traffic/road signs from images. The project uses computer vision and a convolutional neural network (CNN) to recognize different road sign categories.

📌 Project Overview

Road signs play an important role in maintaining road safety by communicating warnings, restrictions, and directions to drivers.

This project aims to build an image classification system that can automatically recognize road signs from input images. The trained model can be used as a foundation for applications such as:

🚗 Driver assistance systems
🛣️ Autonomous driving
📷 Traffic sign recognition
🧠 Computer vision applications
🚦 Intelligent transportation systems
✨ Features
Image-based road sign classification
CNN-based deep learning model
Image preprocessing and normalization
Training and validation pipeline
Prediction on new road sign images
Model evaluation using accuracy and classification metrics
🗂️ Dataset

The model can be trained using a road sign dataset such as the German Traffic Sign Recognition Benchmark (GTSRB).

The dataset contains thousands of labeled traffic sign images belonging to multiple classes.

Example classes include:

Speed Limit
Stop
Yield
No Entry
Priority Road
Turn Right
Turn Left
Pedestrian Crossing
Roundabout
Children Crossing
