🧠 Model Architecture

The classifier uses a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN).

A typical architecture consists of:

Input Image
     ↓
Image Resizing & Normalization
     ↓
Convolutional Layer
     ↓
ReLU Activation
     ↓
Max Pooling
     ↓
Convolutional Layer
     ↓
ReLU Activation
     ↓
Max Pooling
     ↓
Flatten
     ↓
Fully Connected Layer
     ↓
Dropout
     ↓
Softmax
     ↓
Predicted Road Sign


The final Softmax layer produces probabilities for each road sign class.

🚀 Installation

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/krishnNrv06/road-sign-classifier.git
cd road-sign-classifier


Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv venv


Activate it on Windows:

venv\Scripts\activate


On Linux/macOS:

source venv/bin/activate


Install the dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt

🏋️ Training the Model

Prepare the dataset and place it inside the dataset/ directory.

Then run:

python src/train.py


The trained model will be saved in:

models/road_sign_model.h5

🔍 Making Predictions

To classify a new road sign image:

python src/predict.py --image images/sample_sign.jpg


Example output:

Predicted Sign: Speed Limit 50 km/h
Confidence: 96.42%

📊 Model Evaluation

The model can be evaluated using:

Accuracy
Precision
Recall
F1-score
Confusion Matrix

Example:

Test Accuracy: 95.XX%


Replace the example accuracy with the actual result obtained from your trained model.

📷 Example

Input:

sample_sign.jpg


Output:

Predicted Class: Stop Sign
Confidence: 98.15%


You can add screenshots or prediction examples to the images/ directory and display them here:

![Road Sign Prediction](images/sample_sign.jpg)

